  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I got into VRC about last Christmas. I wanted to make avatars, and that needed unity. I had never really done anything with coding or modeling. So I setout to learn unity by the tutorials, and a month later I had a basic 3d pacman game, which I wanted to make a world even though I knew at the time C# was blacklisted. Then I heard about playmaker excitedly bought that. Its a total pain in the ass... But I converted all my C# and more to playmaker eventually. There are not really specific details as to why they didn't go with playmaker. Its crappy but it does work. The thing is though, VRC script is terrible. I would rather drive a nail through my own foreskin. Because at least C# and playmaker have documentation and a community already. VRC script is just hoping you glean tidbits from people you run into with very slim documentation or examples. Or if they are out there, are not centrally linked. \n\n\nI have put a lot of time into my pacman world and I am hopeful these VRC graphs will have the tools to do what I need. But the biggest problem I foresee is that there are complex tools unity has published on GitHub that might not be possible. My world depends on 2 of them.\n\n\nSo if you guys seriously plan on doing this I want to see docs, with examples.\n\nEdit: and for the argument of playmaker being the lynch pin holding things together because its 1 guy... We are still on unity 5.6.3p, which unity stopped developing.",
